markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Alternatives for Restricted Environments

#### If students cannot directly access AI tools, there are still effective ways to teach with AI. Review the strategies below. Regardless of your classroom context, some of these strategies may be helpful for introducing your students to AI.

>#### 💬 **Quick Reflection:** Which, if any, of these would you try in your classroom?

<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 12px; margin-top: 15px;">
  
<!-- Teacher-led demonstrations -->
<div style="background:#fff; padding:15px; text-align:left; border-radius:8px; box-shadow:0 3px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); border:2px solid #5a2ca0; font-size:16px;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/73986745bf0676a2c11ba7999024beee-Screenshot 2026-03-26 at 2.09.25 PM.png" alt="Illustrated classroom scenario involving AI use" style="width:100%; height:175px; object-fit:cover; border-radius:6px; margin-bottom:10px; background:#ececec;">
<strong>Teacher-led demonstrations</strong>
<p style="font-size:14px;">Model AI use in front of the class to make thinking visible.</p>
<ul style="font-size:14px; padding-left:18px; margin:8px 0 0 0;">
<li>Project AI interactions and walk through them together</li>
<li>Model how to ask effective questions and refine prompts</li>
<li>Show how responses change based on different inputs</li>
<li>Think aloud while evaluating accuracy, bias, and usefulness</li>
</ul>
</div>

<!-- Analysis and critique -->
<div style="background:#fff; padding:15px; text-align:left; border-radius:8px; box-shadow:0 3px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); border:2px solid #5a2ca0; font-size:16px;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/f313a04b68c8f7792bedab90ca5d4754-Screenshot 2026-03-26 at 2.09.31 PM.png" alt="Illustrated classroom scenario involving AI use" style="width:100%; height:175px; object-fit:cover; border-radius:6px; margin-bottom:10px; background:#ececec;">
<strong>Analysis and critique of AI outputs</strong>
<p style="font-size:14px;">Use AI-generated content as material for student thinking.</p>
<ul style="font-size:14px; padding-left:18px; margin:8px 0 0 0;">
<li>Provide drafts, explanations, or worked examples for students to analyze</li>
<li>Ask students to critique, revise, or improve AI responses</li>
<li>Compare AI-generated work with student work to identify strengths and limitations</li>
</ul>
</div>

<!-- Simulation and structured practice -->
<div style="background:#fff; padding:15px; text-align:left; border-radius:8px; box-shadow:0 3px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); border:2px solid #5a2ca0; font-size:16px;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/b3a294faf8dcc067f7d4bc9a503293e6-Screenshot 2026-03-26 at 2.09.36 PM.png" alt="Illustrated classroom scenario involving AI use" style="width:100%; height:175px; object-fit:cover; border-radius:6px; margin-bottom:10px; background:#ececec;">
<strong>Simulation and structured practice</strong>
<p style="font-size:14px;">Engage students in AI-like thinking without the tool itself.</p>
<ul style="font-size:14px; padding-left:18px; margin:8px 0 0 0;">
<li>Have students role-play as the “AI” and the “user” to explore how prompts shape responses</li>
<li>Practice evaluating responses and deciding what is useful or not</li>
</ul>
</div>

<!-- Guided practice -->
<div style="background:#fff; padding:15px; text-align:left; border-radius:8px; box-shadow:0 3px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); border:2px solid #5a2ca0; font-size:16px;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/2047c16e4622e48a4d76f7e9c42f49e1-Screenshot 2026-03-26 at 2.09.42 PM.png" alt="Illustrated classroom scenario involving AI use" style="width:100%; height:175px; object-fit:cover; border-radius:6px; margin-bottom:10px; background:#ececec;">
<strong>Guided practice with prompts and responses</strong>
<p style="font-size:14px;">Give students structured opportunities to create, improve, and evaluate AI-style interactions.</p>
<ul style="font-size:14px; padding-left:18px; margin:8px 0 0 0;">
<li>Use sentence starters to help students write prompts</li>
<li>Provide imperfect “AI” responses for students to fix</li>
<li>Sort or rate responses to decide which are most helpful and why</li>
</ul>
</div>

</div>
MARKDOWN
